WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.280
Who else will join Hugh Jackman's Wolverine&nbsp;
in "Deadpool 3?" The Hulk? Maybe Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.599
America? Here's everything we want to&nbsp;
see when the Merc with a Mouth returns.

00:00:09.695 --> 00:00:13.020
When it was first announced that Hugh&nbsp;
Jackman would be back as Wolverine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:16.980
it may have brought about the same sense&nbsp;
of excitement as when actor Josh Brolin was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:21.240
revealed to be taking on the role of Cable&nbsp;
in "Deadpool 2." While his portrayal of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.620
futuristic cyborg warrior was well-received,&nbsp;
many might have been disappointed that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.060
film put Cable into the role of villain for&nbsp;
much of its runtime. Many fans are hoping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.980
that "Deadpool 3" producers won't be tempted to&nbsp;
do the same with Wolverine by pitting the Merc&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:39.600
with a Mouth against the old Canuckle-head,&nbsp;
instead making the film a true team-up.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.580
Given the friendship between actors Ryan Reynolds&nbsp;
and Hugh Jackman, we don't suspect that Wolverine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:49.200
will be Deadpool's enemy, though we do expect&nbsp;
to see at least one fight scene between the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.400
two at some point in the film. Seeing the&nbsp;
two blade-wielding mutants with the fastest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.440
healing factors slicing and dicing away at&nbsp;
one another will surely be a fun sight. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:02.580
if the film is smart, it will dispense with&nbsp;
the rivalry quickly and make Wolverine and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:07.801
Deadpool fast friends, reluctant allies, and&nbsp;
a hard-hitting duo worthy of Jackman's return.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.036
"We work as a team."

00:01:12.036 --> 00:01:16.560
They may adapt a popular storyline from the&nbsp;
comics that saw the pair of X-Men join forces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:21.840
or invent something new for fans to get excited&nbsp;
about. But a proper team-up that lets us see the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:26.921
actors' impeccable on-screen chemistry might be&nbsp;
what fans want to see most out of "Deadpool 3."

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:31.320
With the third "Deadpool" film now under&nbsp;
the Walt Disney banner it's now a realistic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.520
possibility for us to see the inclusion&nbsp;
of characters from the MCU. We're not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.940
sure if that will mean the movie will take&nbsp;
place within the "Avengers" universe or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:42.720
see Deadpool travel through alternate&nbsp;
dimensions, but we fully anticipate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:47.580
at least a couple of MCU cameos. But what we&nbsp;
want to see most is a reunion of the classic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:52.980
"Avengers" team — including the returns of&nbsp;
Iron Man, Captain America, and Black Widow.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:57.720
Though all three characters have met their end in&nbsp;
the MCU, this is "Deadpool" we're talking about,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:02.100
a series where anything goes and nothing&nbsp;
has to make sense. If anything could get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:06.540
Chris Evans or Robert Downey Jr. to make their&nbsp;
way back into costume, we could see them doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:12.060
it for "Deadpool 3," the film that convinced Hugh&nbsp;
Jackman to unretire and dawn his claws once again.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:17.040
Whether it's for a big action sequence or a&nbsp;
blink-and-miss-it cameo like James McAvoy's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.260
"X-Men" in "Deadpool 2," a reunion of "Avengers"&nbsp;
stars feels like the right choice. The chance for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:26.700
Wolverine to meet them is the cherry on top of&nbsp;
the sundae. Even if it's just something silly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:30.500
a comeback for our dearly departed&nbsp;
heroes is what we're hoping for.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.800
We probably speak for all fans when we say&nbsp;
that there's one superficial element that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.960
selfishly want to see for no other reason than its&nbsp;
sheer coolness. That element is a comic-accurate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.280
costume for Hugh Jackman's Wolverine. It's&nbsp;
remarkable to think that Jackman appeared as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:49.500
the character for nearly 20 years, but never wore&nbsp;
any kind of outfit that even vaguely resembles his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.820
traditional comic book costume, and never&nbsp;
once donned his iconic winged face mask.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:59.160
In the most curiously overlooked aspect of the&nbsp;
maverick multi-clawed mutant, fans were teased&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.300
with a possible yellow and black costume in a&nbsp;
deleted scene from "The Wolverine." However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.380
this scene was only included in the home&nbsp;
release of the film. Thus, audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:11.400
missed out on seeing it in action because we&nbsp;
never picked up his story from that point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:16.680
with both "Days of Future Past" and "Logan" taking&nbsp;
place at various points across the timeline.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:21.420
Of course, it would be just like Ryan Reynolds&nbsp;
to know this is exactly what audiences want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:25.980
see and play it for a joke, constantly teasing&nbsp;
a costume that never comes. But in the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:30.720
putting Wolvie in costume is far too tempting&nbsp;
for the notoriously fan-loving Reynolds — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.200
would be too crowd-pleasing a moment&nbsp;
— for him not to include it. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.757
we can't consider this one a lock, we think&nbsp;
it's more than likely the filmmakers deliver.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.418
“You afraid you might like it?"

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:44.820
When it comes to match-ups between a pair&nbsp;
of heroes, few can top Wolverine and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:49.200
Incredible Hulk, a rivalry that began back&nbsp;
in Wolverine's first appearance in "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:55.080
Incredible Hulk" #181. By the late 2000s, both&nbsp;
characters had made their way to the big screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.080 --> 00:04:00.000
with Jackman making Wolverine famous, and&nbsp;
the Hulk appearing in two films of his own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.420
before Mark Ruffalo took on the role&nbsp;
beginning with the superhero team-up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:08.040
film "The Avengers." While rights issues have&nbsp;
kept the characters apart, it hasn't stopped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.700
fans from dreaming about a showdown between&nbsp;
the two actors as their iconic characters.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:16.500
Following Disney's acquisition of Fox, though,&nbsp;
fans began to wonder if their dreams could come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:22.140
true, with Jackman's mutant finally coming to&nbsp;
blows with Ruffalo's monster. Hopes seemed dashed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:26.820
when Jackman doubled down on his retirement&nbsp;
from the role in 2017 after the release of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.780
"Logan." But with the Aussie actor changing&nbsp;
his mind and coming back for "Deadpool 3,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:35.580
we want to see the match-up finally happen,&nbsp;
as it could be our last chance for the Hulk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:40.140
and Wolverine to meet while these two actors&nbsp;
are in the roles. If you ask Mark Ruffalo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:45.060
it could happen, going by his comments on&nbsp;
the Marvelist Podcast in 2018. He said,

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:48.660
"I love Hugh, and it would be cool&nbsp;
to do something with him. If he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:52.658
up to doing it. He's always teased Hulk&nbsp;
versus Wolverine would be pretty fun."

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:57.420
If Ryan Reynolds and writers Paul Wernick and&nbsp;
Rhett Rheese are looking to adapt a story from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:01.920
the comics — one that saw Deadpool and Wolverine&nbsp;
team up — the answer is clearly "The Good,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.820
the Bad, and the Ugly." Named after the&nbsp;
iconic Clint Eastwood spaghetti Western,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:10.980
the 2013 storyline ran in the pages&nbsp;
of "Deadpool" #15 through #19. Full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:15.300
of Deadpool's customary humor, it saw Wade&nbsp;
Wilson enlist the aid of both Wolverine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:19.800
and Captain America in investigating new&nbsp;
information regarding the Weapon X program.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:23.640
Though a movie adaptation would likely&nbsp;
omit Captain America, or maybe not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:28.620
now that Deadpool's under the MCU banner, it&nbsp;
would be easy enough to substitute the Sentinel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:33.660
of Liberty with a character like Colossus or&nbsp;
even Cable. But while the investigation into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:38.400
Weapon X could be compelling, it also could&nbsp;
be a little played out, having been a part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.660
of multiple "X-Men" films. Instead, what we&nbsp;
really love about this story is the spark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:47.280
that sets it off, as a mysterious villain is&nbsp;
caught repeatedly stealing Deadpool's organs.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:51.240
While the Weapon X angle might be a nice&nbsp;
idea to get the two heroes together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:54.900
an organ-theft plot that sees&nbsp;
Deadpool call in Wolverine for help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:59.038
seems like just the kind of sickeningly&nbsp;
twisted story that Reynolds would enjoy.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:04.260
When the dust settled on the acquisition of 20th&nbsp;
Century Fox by the Walt Disney Company in 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:09.780
fans went into a frenzy anticipating a reboot&nbsp;
of the "X-Men" films and their universe within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:14.700
the greater Marvel Cinematic Universe. But it's&nbsp;
been years now and we have yet to see anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:20.760
from the world of mutants in the MCU, with a few&nbsp;
exceptions, including locations like Madripoor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:24.780
in "The Falcon and the Winter Soldier."&nbsp;
However, we may be in for a long wait,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:29.940
as Marvel has revealed its plans for Phase 5&nbsp;
of the MCU, with no "X-Men" on the calendar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:34.980
through at least 2025. But we know they're&nbsp;
coming eventually, so why not include a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:40.498
direct reference to a new team of MCU mutants in&nbsp;
"Deadpool 3" to whet our collective appetites?

00:06:40.801 --> 00:06:45.060
She-Hulk is a bit more of a longshot,&nbsp;
especially considering the divisive fan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:49.500
reaction to the Disney+ series. But there's&nbsp;
been talk that She-Hulk will be making her way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:53.760
to the big screen eventually, according&nbsp;
to The Direct. So there's no reason she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:58.020
can't get a head start with an appearance in&nbsp;
"Deadpool 3." A longtime fourth-wall breaker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:01.140
Jennifer Walters' habit of turning&nbsp;
to the camera and talking directly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:05.520
to the audience predates "Deadpool" in the&nbsp;
comics, and continues to be used to great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.720
comedic effect in her own series. We believe&nbsp;
seeing them sharing the screen and arguing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:13.860
over which one is going to get the audience's&nbsp;
attention, would be a recipe for comedy gold.

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:17.640
And while much of the silliness in "She-Hulk"&nbsp;
may not have been a hit with audiences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:20.160
her tongue-in-cheek humor could feel right at home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:24.098
in "Deadpool," where a twerk or a&nbsp;
"bruh" might not be out of place.

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:25.200
"Bruh."

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:29.820
Plus, if we do get a Hulk/Wolverine showdown,&nbsp;
who better to break it up than Bruce's cousin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:34.618
who can mock the overly macho boys for always&nbsp;
finding a reason to fight amongst themselves?

00:07:34.618 --> 00:07:38.760
Heading into the release of "Doctor Strange&nbsp;
in the Multiverse of Madness," many fans were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:43.920
hoping for a parade of former movie guest stars.&nbsp;
There were big dreams of seeing non-MCU heroes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:48.180
like Nicolas Cage's Ghost Rider or Wesley&nbsp;
Snipes' Blade back in action across the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:52.560
multiverse. There was even brief talk of&nbsp;
new versions of the Avengers, with rumors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:58.076
swirling of Tom Cruise suiting up as Iron Man –&nbsp;
gossip that turned out to be entirely made up.

00:07:58.459 --> 00:07:59.839
"Nice!"

00:07:59.839 --> 00:08:03.660
Ultimately, though, the film limited its&nbsp;
guest appearances to the Illuminati in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:07.680
a single key sequence, disappointing&nbsp;
many. But if "Deadpool" is truly going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:10.740
to embrace the weirdness of being&nbsp;
under the Disney and MCU banners,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:15.960
cameos from heroes from past movie universes&nbsp;
would be the perfect card to play. Admittedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:19.920
we don't want "Deadpool 3" to get bogged down&nbsp;
in cameos, but that doesn't mean they can't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:23.460
give them to us in spades while keeping&nbsp;
the movie focused on a streamlined story.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:28.140
After all, there's no better franchise to&nbsp;
utilize one-off appearances from a gaggle of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:32.880
multiverse heroes than this one, where a joke&nbsp;
can be played for a laugh before moving on. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:37.980
cavalcade of cameos would finally fulfill every&nbsp;
fan's fantasies. The opportunity to have Hugh&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:42.900
Jackman's Wolverine finally share the screen with&nbsp;
the likes of Ioan Gruffudd's Mr. Fantastic — or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:47.371
even Ben Affleck's Daredevil — in single-scene&nbsp;
gags might be too tempting to pass up.

00:08:47.371 --> 00:08:50.820
The internet and social media have been&nbsp;
blowing up since the announcement that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:54.780
Hugh Jackman would be back as Wolverine&nbsp;
for "Deadpool 3." Hordes of fans have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:59.160
assembling their wish lists of cameos and&nbsp;
match-ups. But in all the excitement over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:03.180
the unprecedented access the filmmakers&nbsp;
have to any number of Marvel heroes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:07.920
we want to make sure they don't forget that&nbsp;
Deadpool already has an excellent supporting cast.

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:10.560
That's right, with all the&nbsp;
talk centered on Wolverine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:14.220
let's remember there are plenty of great&nbsp;
characters from the first two films we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:19.080
want to see back in action. That includes&nbsp;
disgruntled cabbie Dopinder, lucky Domino,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:25.980
steel-skinned Colossus, sardonic roommate Blind&nbsp;
Al, and the jaded Negasonic Teenage Warhead. Heck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:30.480
we might even get to see fire-starter Rusty&nbsp;
Collins and time-traveling mutant Cable too.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:33.900
Let's face it: we want to see cameos,&nbsp;
but only as long as the film doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:38.520
get sidetracked so far that it forgets about&nbsp;
old favorites. Some fans might worry that so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:42.720
many characters will hurt the film, but Marvel&nbsp;
has excelled with large ensemble casts before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:46.920
and even a solo film or two with plenty of&nbsp;
guests. They can watch "Captain America:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:50.917
Civil War" or "Spider-Man: No Way Home"&nbsp;
if they want to see how to do it right.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:55.680
No joke, we want to see Kevin Feige. Yes,&nbsp;
we mean the President of Marvel Studios,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.680 --> 00:10:00.000
the master of the Marvel Cinematic Universe,&nbsp;
and the man with the famous baseball cap.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.720
We want to see him in "Deadpool 3."&nbsp;
How and why, you ask? For starters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:08.100
he's the king of all things Marvel movies, and&nbsp;
it's long past due that the fans get a chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:12.600
to show their love. "Deadpool 3," the first&nbsp;
film to firmly cross over the "X-Men" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:16.980
MCU universes with a sense of good humor,&nbsp;
is just the right place for it to happen.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:22.140
Don't forget, Marvel Comics founder Stan Lee has&nbsp;
had cameos in nearly every major Marvel movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:26.760
and with his passing in 2018, maybe&nbsp;
Marvel can pass the torch to Feige,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:32.040
the founder of the MCU. A movie that doesn't just&nbsp;
break the fourth wall but smashes through it could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:36.660
easily see its star breaking down Feige's door&nbsp;
and demanding answers when he finds himself in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:42.240
the MCU, unaware of Disney's purchase of 20th&nbsp;
Century Fox. It might even combine our wish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:46.935
for an "X-Men" reboot tease with the studio head&nbsp;
knee-deep in franchise planning when we see him.

00:10:47.039 --> 00:10:47.879
"That'll do!"

